# The zmx wire protocol byte (PROTOCOL_VERSION in vendor/zmx/src/ipc.zig) that meum's bundled zmx speaks.
#
# Terminals outlive meum: their zmx daemons keep running across a quit and an update. A meum whose zmx speaks a
# different byte can't talk to the daemons the previous version started; after the update every surviving session
# would be unreachable and meum would open fresh shells beside the orphaned ones.
#
# So the byte is recorded here. scripts/build-app.sh refuses a zmx whose byte differs from this file, and
# scripts/release.sh --publish refuses a release whose byte differs from the last public one unless it is given
# --zmx-protocol-change. Before changing it, make the new meum able to reach the old daemons (keep the previous
# zmx as bin/zmx-<byte> and attach with the binary the daemon was started from), or accept losing the sessions.
1
